 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "The rules",
   "span": "full",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "table",
     "class": "methods",
     "head": [
      "Rule",
      "What it gives",
      "Example"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "Angle sum $180°(n-2)$",
       "from one corner: $n-2$ triangles",
       "heptagon: $5\\cdot180°=900°$"
      ],
      [
       "Every extra side adds $180°$",
       "compare two polygons fast",
       "12 and 9 sides: $3\\cdot180°=540°$"
      ],
      [
       "From the sum to $n$",
       "sum $\\div180°$ = triangles, then $+2$",
       "$900°\\div180°=5$, so $7$ sides"
      ],
      [
       "**Regular** = all sides AND all angles equal",
       "one angle $=\\frac{180°(n-2)}{n}=180°-\\frac{360°}{n}$",
       "$108°$, $120°$, $135°$"
      ],
      [
       "Central angle = exterior angle $=\\frac{360°}{n}$",
       "it completes the angle to $180°$",
       "octagon: $45°+135°=180°$"
      ],
      [
       "All the exterior angles: $360°$",
       "one angle given: exterior first",
       "$160°$: $20°$, so $360\\div20=18$ sides"
      ],
      [
       "Diagonals from one corner (regular)",
       "cut its angle into **equal** parts",
       "pentagon $3\\cdot36°$, hexagon $4\\cdot30°$"
      ],
      [
       "Angle at a corner, arms through corners (regular)",
       "$\\frac{180°}{n}$ for every side between the arms",
       "10 sides, 3 between: $3\\cdot18°=54°$"
      ],
      [
       "Radii (regular)",
       "$n$ isosceles triangles; hexagon: 6 equilateral, radius = side",
       "pentagon: $72°$, $54°$, $54°$"
      ],
      [
       "Corner triangle (two sides + a diagonal)",
       "isosceles: base angles $\\frac{180°-\\text{angle}}{2}$",
       "pentagon $36°$, hexagon $30°$"
      ],
      [
       "Regular hexagon, side $a$",
       "short diagonal $a\\sqrt3$, long diagonal $2a$",
       "$a=5$: $5\\sqrt3$ and $10$"
      ],
      [
       "Diagonals from one corner: $n-3$",
       "all of them: $\\frac{n(n-3)}{2}$ (two ends each)",
       "10 sides: $\\frac{10\\cdot7}{2}=35$"
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
